  "id": "DrugBank_DB09074 - MONDO_6335",
  "verbalization": "Olaparib, a poly (ADP-ribose) polymerase inhibitor, is linked to Ovarian Endometrioid Adenocarcinoma through a series of indications that suggest its potential use in treating this cancer. The evidence shows that Olaparib is indicated for Immature Ovarian Teratomas, which are benign tumors, and that these tumors are associated with Carboplatin and Melphalan, both of which are used in cancer treatment. This creates a chain of indications that ultimately points to Ovarian Endometrioid Adenocarcinoma as a target. The mechanism is not explicitly stated, but the shared use of chemotherapy agents in the chain implies a possible role in the treatment of this cancer. The evidence is consistent across different paths, suggesting a potential pathway where Olaparib may influence the treatment of Ovarian Endometrioid Adenocarcinoma through its interaction with chemotherapy regimens.",
